        "title": "fix: land nine small correctness fixes",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nNine small contributor fixes were individually correct but based on pre-rewrite `main` histories that cannot be safely refreshed through GitHub's verified fork-edit path. This takeover preserves each fix as a focused commit with its original contributor in a `Co-authored-by` trailer.\n\nSources: #99727, #99938, #96417, #100110, #100020, #99580, #99514, #98771, #99400.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Preserve literal dollar sequences during memory-wiki reimport.\n- Handle Tailscale cleanup spawn errors.\n- Reject invalid response byte limits at the canonical HTTP-body owner.\n- Match listening ports exactly instead of by prefix.\n- Keep exec/gateway truncation on UTF-16 boundaries using the canonical normalization helper.\n- Reject surrogate numeric HTML entities.\n- Guard Claude Fable 5 prefix matching at model-id boundaries.\n- Render model context windows in decimal K.\n- Preserve non-Error ClickClack websocket rejection diagnostics.\n\nEach source diff was replayed onto current `main`; #96417 was adapted to the consolidated HTTP-body owner, and #100020 was fixed to use `@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice` after remote proof caught its stale helper import.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThese are narrow correctness and diagnostics fixes across memory import, voice-call cleanup, HTTP limits, port inspection, output truncation, HTML decoding, Anthropic routing, model display, and ClickClack gateway failures. No new config or compatibility surface.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Crabbox AWS `cbx_191d15c9f081`, run `run_8f69182f8f84`: 9 Vitest shards passed, 215 tests total; lease stopped.\n- Fresh Codex autoreview after fixups: clean, no actionable findings.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Repo formatter applied to the two canonical UTF-16 helper imports.\n\nThe first Crabbox run (`cbx_19c9d978dbc8`) correctly failed because #100020 referenced a helper removed by the `main` rewrite; the takeover now imports the canonical normalization-core helper and the identical rerun passed.\n",
